---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
// The chat disclosure is owner-approved language with exactly one source. It is
// rendered here and on /deep-kore from this same constant so the two can never drift.
import { PRIVACY_DISCLOSURE } from '../data/deep-kore';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Privacy policy for the ByteLite LLC website: what is collected, what is never collected, and how to request deletion."
  keywords="ByteLite LLC privacy policy"
  
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <!--
        The page's own revision marker. It must move whenever the policy changes
        materially, because the "Changes to this policy" section below promises exactly
        that. Updated 2026-09-01 for the live chat disclosure.
      -->
      <p class="legal-sub">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-body">

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>ByteLite LLC is committed to privacy as a design requirement, not a legal checkbox. This policy describes what data is collected through this website and under what conditions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>What this website collects</h2>
        <h3>Contact form submissions</h3>
        <p>If you submit the contact form, your name, email address, inquiry type, message, and optionally an organization name are submitted to an endpoint on this site. Your IP address is used to enforce a submission rate limit. This data is used solely to respond to your inquiry. It is not sold, shared with third parties, or used for marketing.</p>
        <p>Delivery uses SendGrid, a third-party transactional email provider, which processes the message in order to send it. There is no CRM and no marketing automation: the message becomes an email to ByteLite LLC and nothing else. Submissions are validated server-side, and a failed submission tells you it failed rather than silently discarding your message.</p>
        <h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p><strong>No analytics provider is currently loaded on this website.</strong> No Google Analytics tag, no other analytics script, and no advertising or tracking script is served by any page. If privacy-respecting analytics are added in future, they will run only where you have recorded consent through the cookie preferences described below, and this policy will be updated before that happens.</p>
        <h3>The live chat</h3>
        <p><strong>The live chat on this website is switched off at the server unless ByteLite LLC has explicitly enabled it.</strong> While it is off, a request to start a session is refused and nothing you could type is sent anywhere.</p>
        {/*
          The owner-approved disclosure, imported from src/data/deep-kore.ts and rendered
          verbatim. The identical sentence appears on /deep-kore, and a test asserts both
          match. Never paraphrase it here: a promise made on the page and the policy
          recording it must not differ.
        */}
        <p>{PRIVACY_DISCLOSURE}</p>
        <p>What you type is sent to an endpoint on this site, and from there to a protected Deep Kore system operated by ByteLite LLC. <strong>It is not sent to any third-party AI provider, because there is not one:</strong> no external model, hosted or otherwise, is used at any point, and no scripted or canned answer stands in when the system cannot be reached.</p>
        <p>Your IP address is seen by the hosting provider in the ordinary course of serving the request, and is passed to Cloudflare Turnstile only if a human check is in use. Errors are recorded by type only. Prompts, responses, session identifiers and credentials are not written to any log.</p>
        <p><strong>The conversation is not connected to anything else you do on this site.</strong> Chat content is not linked to a contact-form submission, a founder reservation, a Supporter Pack purchase, or anything held by Stripe, and none of those records is available to the chat. There is no account, no profile and no identifier that joins them.</p>
        <p><strong>The transcript you can see lives only in the page.</strong> It is held in the browser tab's memory for as long as the page is open, and it is not written to local storage, session storage, IndexedDB or any file. Reloading the page or navigating away clears it. No analytics or third-party service receives any part of it, because none is loaded on this website at all. Each response can show a short technical record of how it was handled, including an opaque reference for any idea the system settled during that turn. The reference cannot be turned back into the idea it stands for, means nothing outside your conversation, and stops meaning anything once the session ends.</p>
        <h3>Context you choose to give</h3>
        <p>The live chat includes an optional panel in which you can describe how you are related to a person or place you want to ask about. <strong>Nothing there is worked out from your messages</strong> - every fact is one you deliberately entered or chose from a fixed list, and ordinary conversation works without any of it.</p>
        <p>What you enter is kept in your browser tab's memory and nowhere else. <strong>The name you use for someone is never transmitted</strong>: it exists so you can recognise your own entries, and what is sent is an anonymous reference plus the relationship you chose. All of it is discarded when the session ends, when the conversation cannot continue, and when you leave the page, and you can remove any of it at any time.</p>
        <h3>Values you keep on your own device</h3>
        <p>Having that context, the system may ask for one specific fact by name - a phone number, an address - because answering requires stating it back. If you choose to enter such a value it is kept in your browser tab's memory: it is not written to your device's storage, not placed in the conversation you can see, and not included in anything submitted for review.</p>
        <p><strong>You decide whether it is sent.</strong> Nothing is preselected, and taking no action sends nothing. If you send it, it is transmitted to ByteLite LLC's own system for that <strong>one answer</strong> and then discarded - it is not retained, and the same question asked later has to ask you again. If you decline, no value is transmitted at all and the conversation continues. The value is cleared after that single use, on refusal, when you remove it, when the session ends, when the conversation cannot continue, and when you leave the page.</p>
        <p>It is not sent to any third party at any point: there is no external model, and no analytics, advertising or logging system on this website receives it.</p>
        <h3>Concepts submitted for review</h3>
        <p>If the system does not recognise something in your message, you may be offered the choice to submit it for review. That choice is separate, explicit, specific to that one item, and refused by default; declining stores nothing at all.</p>
        <p>If you consent, an unverified candidate is stored in a review queue for ByteLite LLC to examine later. <strong>It does not become part of what the system knows.</strong> Consenting authorises storage and nothing else - it does not teach the system, does not make the item correct, and does not activate it; only ByteLite LLC, acting separately, can decide what to do with a candidate. Your message text, the conversation, and any private value you kept on your device are not stored with it.</p>
        <h3>Cookies and local storage</h3>
        <p>This website does not set advertising cookies. It stores your cookie-consent choice in your browser's local storage so the consent banner does not reappear on every page. Clearing your browser storage for this site removes it.</p>
        <p>If you start a live chat session, two cookies are set for that session and for nothing else: an essential session cookie identifying the session, which your browser's scripts cannot read, and one used to confirm that a request came from this page rather than another site. Both are host-only and marked secure, both are forgotten when your browser session ends, and choosing "End and delete session" clears them immediately. Neither is used for tracking, and no chat cookie is set unless you start a session.</p>
        <p>Nothing else from a conversation is placed in your browser's storage. The chat writes no message, response, private value, relationship you described, or review candidate to local storage, session storage or IndexedDB.</p>
        <h3>Consents are separate, and stay separate</h3>
        <p>Starting a conversation, describing a relationship in the context panel, sending a private value for one answer, submitting an unrecognised concept for review, contacting ByteLite LLC, purchasing, and any future marketing all require their own decision. <strong>None of them is bundled with another, and agreeing to one never implies agreeing to any of the others.</strong> Sending a value once is never permission to send it again.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
        <ul class="legal-list">
          <li>Sell personal information to third parties</li>
          <li>Create advertising profiles</li>
          <li>Track individuals across other websites</li>
          <li>Use behavioral targeting advertising</li>
          <li>Load any analytics or tracking script</li>
          <li>Retain contact form data beyond the purpose of responding</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Other ByteLite LLC services</h2>
        <p>This website is about ByteLite. ByteLite LLC also operates separate, non-public services that are not presented on this site but that do process data, and they are disclosed here so this policy stays complete.</p>
        <p><strong>Cordel Connect.</strong> This application is in private Android test and beta development only. It is not available on any public app store. A separate, app-specific privacy policy will be published before any broader beta release or public app launch. Beta participants are informed of data handling specific to their testing role. Nothing about that testing is collected through this website.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Payments and founder reservations</h2>
        <p><strong>Nothing on this website charges you today.</strong> Every founder control is switched off at the server, not merely hidden, and a request to start a checkout is refused rather than processed.</p>
        <p><strong>When it is enabled, payment is handled by Stripe.</strong> Card details are entered on Stripe's own hosted checkout page. ByteLite LLC never receives, sees or stores your card number, in test mode or live mode. Stripe processes that data as its own controller under its own privacy policy.</p>
        <p><strong>What ByteLite LLC would retain</strong> for a reservation or purchase is deliberately small: which product and plan you chose, which version of the founder offer you accepted, and which version of the terms applied. That is what is needed to honour the offer later and to account for the transaction. It does not include your card details.</p>
        <p><strong>Supporter wall listing is separate and off by default.</strong> If the Founder Supporter Pack is ever purchased, appearing on a public supporter wall happens only if you tick a separate, unticked box and choose a display name. Agreeing to a purchase is never agreeing to be listed, and neither is agreeing to marketing - there is no marketing list.</p>
        <p>Removal from a supporter wall, or withdrawal of a reservation, can be requested through the contact page at any time.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>This website is served by a third-party hosting provider, which necessarily processes request data such as IP addresses in the ordinary course of serving pages. Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts. SendGrid delivers contact-form messages. Stripe is the payment processor for founder reservations and the Founder Supporter Pack, and is currently operating in <strong>test mode</strong> with all checkout controls disabled. Cloudflare provides the network path to the Deep Kore system behind the live chat, and Cloudflare Turnstile provides the human check where one is in use. ByteLite LLC does not use advertising networks on this website, and no advertising or tracking script is served by any page.</p>
        <p><strong>No third-party AI or model provider is used anywhere on this website.</strong> The live chat is answered by a ByteLite LLC system and by nothing else, and there is no external model behind it or beside it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>You may request deletion of any contact form data submitted by emailing through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. ByteLite LLC will respond within a reasonable timeframe.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>This policy may be updated as ByteLite LLC's products develop. The updated date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be noted.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Privacy questions may be directed through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. ByteLite LLC is based in Helena, Montana, USA.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>

.legal-hero { padding: 5rem 0 3.5rem; }
.legal-hero h1 { max-width: 480px; }
.legal-sub { margin-top: .75rem; font-size: .9375rem; color: #555e7a; }
.legal-body { max-width: 760px; }
.legal-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
.legal-section h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-bottom: .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a2235; }
.legal-section h3 { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin: 1.5rem 0 .5rem; }
.legal-section p { font-size: .9375rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: .875rem; }
.legal-section a { color: #818cf8; }
.legal-section a:hover { color: #a5b4fc; }
.legal-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .625rem; }
.legal-list li { font-size: .9375rem; color: #7b829e; padding-left: 1.25rem; position: relative; line-height: 1.6; }
.legal-list li::before { content: "-"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: #4a5068; }

</style>
